    "title": "Zambian president Hichilema has early lead in reelection bid | AP International | swoknews.com",
    "text": "Zambia’s president maintained an early lead in elections in which he’s seeking to extend his rule of the copper-rich southern African nation.\nHakainde Hichilema garnered 438,708 votes in 49 of the country’s 226 constituencies announced by the Electoral Commission of Zambia late Saturday. His closest rival, opposition leader Brian Mundubile, obtained 351,281, it said. Voter turnout was around 55%, down from about 70% in the last general election.",
